comment1.target=SlotMachine()
comment1.text=\r\n Constructor for objects of class SlotMachine. Paces the\r\n step-by-step animation in spin(wheel, steps) with a plain\r\n Thread.sleep.\r\n
comment10.params=wheel
comment10.target=void spin(int)
comment10.text=\r\n Turn only the indicated wheel.\r\n
comment11.target=void spin()
comment11.text=\r\n Turn all the wheels on the machine.\r\n
comment12.target=java.lang.String[] symbols()
comment12.text=\r\n List the colors of all the machines\r\n
comment13.target=int distinctSymbols()
comment13.text=\r\n number of different colors on all the roulette wheels.\r\n
comment14.target=java.lang.String[] configuration()
comment14.text=\r\n Visible colors on each wheel, from left to right.\r\n
comment15.target=boolean isJackpot()
comment15.text=\r\n true if all wheels display the same symbol.\r\n This is a plain, deterministic comparison of the current\r\n configuration\: it does not depend on chance in any way, only the\r\n spin that produced that configuration does (see Wheel.spin()).\r\n
comment16.target=boolean ok()
comment16.text=\r\n @return true if the last operation was succeed\r\n
comment17.target=void succeed()
comment18.params=reason
comment18.target=void fail(java.lang.String)
comment18.text=\r\n Marks the last operation as failed and, if the simulator is\r\n visible, shows the reason to the user through a JOptionPane.\r\n
comment19.target=void announceJackpotIfReached()
comment19.text=\r\n If the machine is visible and just reached a winning configuration,\r\n congratulate the user through a JOptionPane.\r\n
comment2.params=pacer
comment2.target=SlotMachine(StepPacer)
comment2.text=\r\n Constructor for objects of class SlotMachine, letting the caller\r\n decide how the step-by-step animation in spin(wheel, steps) is\r\n paced.\r\n\r\n @param pacer used to pause between animation steps.\r\n
comment20.target=void rebuildShapes()
comment20.text=\r\n (Re)builds the machine's body, the jackpot light and one square per\r\n wheel. Called whenever the number of wheels changes.\r\n
comment21.target=void refreshShapes()
comment21.text=\r\n Repaints the wheels' squares, the jackpot light and the machine's\r\n body to match the current configuration.\r\n
comment22.target=void syncVisualState()
comment22.text=\r\n Shows or hides every shape according to the visible flag, and keeps\r\n the jackpot light on only while the machine is visible and won.\r\n
comment23.params=value min max
comment23.target=int clamp(int, int, int)
comment24.target=void exit()
comment25.params=wheel1 wheel2
comment25.target=void swap(int, int)
comment25.text=\r\n exchanges the positions of two roulette wheels. \r\n It temporarily saves the first wheel in memory, moves the second wheel \r\n into the first wheel's slot, and \r\n then assigns the saved copy of the first wheel to the second wheel's original \r\n slot.\r\n
